            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "naples34102"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Loved, loved, loved this! The seasonings are classic and perfect but it was the cooking method that particularly impressed me. I generally prepare shrimp this way in a skillet on the stove top, but this was just too easy! What was really kind of cool was that I used three shrimp apiece as an appetizer for our grilled steak dinner using small gratin dishes that looked so pretty on the serving plate along with the steaks! For additional flavor and color I added chopped fresh chives from my garden and sprinkled the shrimp with paprika. I know I'll be repeating this as an easy and delicious appetizer regularly."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Gail Denver"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made exactly as mentioned. I always soak my raw shrimp in lemon water before cooking. Gives them a nice flavor.",
            "datePublished": "2022-08-11T00:59:23.514Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ang"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Awesome! I am doing a Whole30, so I substituted ghee for the butter. The shrimp I used was cooked, tail-off, deveined and peeled already so after thawing it, I tossed it in the mixture. I also added paprika, Old Bay seasoning, and lemon juice. I let it marinate for about 20 minutes and then heated the mixture in a saute pan. Once I saw tendrils of steam and the liquid slightly bubbling, I turned off the heat. As all the reviews say- simple and delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2014-05-14T18:00:55.113Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Strawberry Blonde"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent! Super easy. I baked the shrimp for 5 extra minutes and upped the temp to 375 the last 5. I also made extra scampi sauce to toss in angel hair. Delicious.",
            "datePublished": "2025-10-08T01:56:55.868Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Stephen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've made this a few times now, and it's been a hit. I followed the recommendations of several of the other commenters, including reducing the butter, adding about 1/3 c of white wine, some extra garlic, lemon juice, and parsley. Served over linguine. Also, in a pinch, I don't do the arranging, and I use parchment to save on clean up. Definitely a hit!",
            "datePublished": "2020-05-11T23:00:18.457Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "NH Grammy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "2 lbs lg shrimp, defrost in fridge from Sat morning till Monday supper. Melt 4 TBL butter, add 4 cloves garlic, 2.5 TBL olive oil and 187 ml Barefoot pinot grigio and the juice of 1 lemon. Marinate shrimp 15 minutes or longer. Bake in single layer in lg glass dish, 15-20 min at 350 degrees. Fantastic. 2.1.16",
            "datePublished": "2016-02-01T17:49:40.030Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Bayla Meltzer"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made it tonight for supper and while it was good, it was a bit bland. Next time, I’ll add more garlic and salt and maybe add some oregano. But it was super fast and easy to throw together.\nUPDATE: increased salt to 1.5 tsps salt, 3 big cloves garlic and 1/4 tsp oregano....Delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2020-01-06T23:31:30.740Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "nochef"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I doubled the garlic upped the butter and cut the oil, upped the salt and and added red pepper flakes as per previous reviews. I also put this over thin spaghetti. It was a great quick dinner.",
            "datePublished": "2023-11-30T01:35:40.754Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Bobbie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made this after reading comments of other reviewers, so I took some their suggestions to add some wine, lemon and panko crumbs for crunch. I did take off the tails as my husband doesn't like doing that. Let the shrimp marinade for about a half hour in the sauce before baking. Served over bow tie pasta with a little shredded Parmesan cheese and some rosemary garlic bread. It was his birthday dinner and he had 2 helpings. I think as written, it'd be very good, but the suggestions makes it 5 star.",
            "datePublished": "2018-03-04T19:02:12.610Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Diane R"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I make this at least once a month. The seasonings with oil are a perfect combination. My only addition is that I top off with about 6-10 halved grape tomatoes before baking. I love the fact that they can be done in the oven. I have served this over pasta and, for me, it is so much easier than sauteeing the scampi on the stove top. Fifteen minutes in the oven gives me just enough time to cook the pasta, toss the salad, etc.",
            "datePublished": "2025-09-29T13:48:37.884Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MPEBLE"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Note: If the shrimp are starting from frozen, you'll need significantly longer than ten minutes in the oven. I suggest 400 degrees and covering the top of the casserole dish loosely with foil so the shrimp gently steam with the butter.",
            "datePublished": "2016-10-24T03:13:07.923Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "wrblogs"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The balance of flavors is simply perfect—savory garlic, zesty lemon, and a touch of white wine create a luxurious, restaurant-quality dish. The shrimp are tender and juicy, and soak up all the delicious flavors.",
